# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Neon PostgreSQL connection string
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your real Neon connection string.
# The `.env` file is gitignored so your credentials never land on GitHub.
#
# Format:
#   NEON_CONNECTION_STRING=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DBNAME?sslmode=require
#
# On Vercel: set this same value as a Project Environment Variable
# (https://vercel.com/med-ba1c/erp-mauritania/settings/environment-variables)
# Note: the `postgres` package uses dart:io sockets which do NOT work on
# Flutter Web. On web builds the DatabaseService automatically falls
# back to the in-memory store. To use Neon from web, deploy a serverless
# HTTP API (Vercel Functions / Supabase) and adapt DatabaseService to
# call it via HTTP instead of the postgres package.
NEON_CONNECTION_STRING=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/dbname?sslmode=require
